+/**
+ * Dump a PFR font's glyphs to the client's atlas JSON, rasterised through the
+ * SAME path Director used at runtime: `BitmapFont::fromPfr1(pfr, size)`, i.e.
+ * `FontRegistry::getPfrBitmapFont` / `SimpleTextRenderer`. FontProbe shows this
+ * path reproduces the original's on-screen metrics (cell, cap height, advances),
+ * where both `PfrToAtlas` (its own grid-fit rasteriser) and a GDI pass over the
+ * converted TTF come out a pixel short and mis-proportioned.
+ *
+ *   libreshockwave_bitmapfont_to_atlas <font.pfr> <size> <out.json> [--soft]
+ *
+ * Emits the same schema `tools/build-glyph-atlas.ps1` and `PfrToAtlas` do, so
+ * the client's `lingo-glyph-atlas` loads it without knowing which produced it.
+ * Aliased (1-bit) by default, matching a member with `the antiAlias` off; pass
+ * `--soft` to keep the rasteriser's coverage for antialiased members.
